# Road-chain placement validation

Update valid road placement so a new road may connect to an owned road as well as an owned settlement or city.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] A road adjoining a road of the same colour is valid.
- [x] A road adjoining a settlement or city of the same colour remains valid.
- [x] A road adjoining only opponent-owned roads/buildings remains invalid.
- [x] A disconnected road remains invalid.
- [x] Board editing and projected construction-plan editing use the same revised rule.
- [x] Earlier planned roads count when validating a later road step.
- [x] Invalid placement shows exactly `Road must be adjacent to a road, settlement or city of the same colour.` for two seconds.
- [x] Existing ownership, removal, serialization, and building-distance behavior remains unchanged.
- [x] Domain and UI regression bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This task supersedes TASK-012's literal building-only interpretation of the earlier REQ-012 wording.
- Connectivity is satisfied when either endpoint touches an owned building or an existing/planned owned road sharing that endpoint.

